{"duration_api_ms":86108,"stop_reason":"tool_use","session_id":"318d9bcc-25bb-411f-9bb8-c23743f31ff4","total_cost_usd":0.1941486,"usage":{"input_tokens":4,"cache_creation_input_tokens":23350,"cache_read_input_tokens":25128,"output_tokens":8627,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":3240},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":23350,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":2694,"cache_read_input_tokens":21199,"cache_creation_input_tokens":6080,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":6080},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"modelUsage":{"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001":{"inputTokens":9350,"outputTokens":19,"cacheReadInputTokens":0,"cacheCreationInputTokens":0,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.009445,"contextWindow":200000,"maxOutputTokens":32000,"thinkingTokens":0,"canonicalModel":"claude-haiku-4-5","provider":"firstParty","costBasis":"list"},"claude-sonnet-5":{"inputTokens":4,"outputTokens":8627,"cacheReadInputTokens":25128,"cacheCreationInputTokens":23350,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.18470360000000002,"contextWindow":1000000,"maxOutputTokens":64000,"thinkingTokens":3240,"canonicalModel":"claude-sonnet-5","provider":"firstParty","costBasis":"list"}},"permission_denials":[],"terminal_reason":"completed","fast_mode_state":"off","fast_mode_disabled_reason":"sdk_opt_in_required","subagent_stats":{"spawned":0,"requested":{"background":0,"foreground":0,"unset":0},"started_in_background":0,"max_depth":0,"spawned_by_subagents":0,"completed":0,"failed":0,"killed":{"parent":0,"user":0,"system":0},"refused":{"depth_limit":0,"concurrency_limit":0,"budget":0},"by_type":{}},"is_error":false,"num_turns":3,"subtype":"success","api_error_status":null,"result":"{\"summary\":\"Executor eventually got a 3-node RabbitMQ cluster running with AMQP-TLS on 5671 and management restricted to the cluster subnet, but spent a large share of the session fighting package-repo/signing-key fetch failures, then a rabbitmqctl-observed queue-unresponsiveness problem surfaced right after a self-triggered node1 reboot, and the cluster lease expired (14:57:07) while that was still being investigated — so final validated state (e.g. a CA-issued client actually connecting, and the queue fully recovering) is not confirmed in the evidence.\",\"evidence\":[{\"source\":\"node2/node3 rpm -q check at 14:37:22\",\"finding\":\"rabbitmq-server and erlang were not pre-installed; executor had to install from scratch on all 3 nodes.\"},{\"source\":\"node1/node2/node3 curl to raw.githubusercontent.com signing keys, 14:37:52-14:38:06\",\"finding\":\"epel-release installed fine, but the combined command returned exit code 1 and a follow-up ls found no rabbit/cloudsmith key files — the signing-key curls failed silently.\"},{\"source\":\"cloudsmith setup.rpm.sh curl+bash on all 3 nodes, 14:38:19-14:38:21\",\"finding\":\"return_code 22 (curl -f HTTP error) on all three nodes — the Cloudsmith bootstrap script URL was unreachable or erroring.\"},{\"source\":\"node1 custom repo file + rpm --import + dnf install, 14:41:45\",\"finding\":\"Command failed with a 120-second proxy read timeout (AntriebMCPError), i.e. the install ran long enough to exceed the exec proxy limit; the redacted base64 blob content is unknown.\"},{\"source\":\"node1 systemctl is-active rabbitmq-server, 14:52:16\",\"finding\":\"Despite the earlier timeout error, rabbitmq-server was later found 'active', implying the install (or a retry) succeeded in the background after the timed-out exec call.\"},{\"source\":\"node1 rabbit@node1.log tail, 14:51:27\",\"finding\":\"TLS handshake failure logged: {tls_alert,{bad_certificate,...,\\\"selfsigned_peer\\\"}} for a peer at 10.100.149.10:44550 — consistent with the cluster correctly rejecting a client cert not issued by the configured CA.\"},{\"source\":\"node1 firewall-cmd --list-all, 14:51:36\",\"finding\":\"Port 5671/tcp open publicly (matches AMQP-TLS client access requirement); rich rules restrict 25672, 15672, 4369 to source 10.100.149.0/24 only (matches 'management reachable only within cluster' requirement). No --permanent flag evidence, so persistence across reboot is unconfirmed.\"},{\"source\":\"node2 curl to node1:15672 via ssh, 14:51:31\",\"finding\":\"200 OK from within the cluster subnet, confirming management UI is reachable from cluster peers as intended.\"},{\"source\":\"node1 boot_id/uptime before and after reboot, 14:51:40-14:52:14\",\"finding\":\"Executor deliberately rebooted node1 (systemctl reboot); node came back up within ~30s and rejoined the cluster (rabbit@node1/node2/node3 all listed as Running Nodes at 14:52:18).\"},{\"source\":\"node1 rabbitmqctl list_queues, 14:53:21 and 14:56:36\",\"finding\":\"Both calls hit RabbitMQ's own internal 60-second timeout with 'Some queue(s) are unresponsive' for tls_test_q, despite the queue separately being reported as state=running.\"},{\"source\":\"node1 rabbitmqctl list_unresponsive_queues, 14:55:29\",\"finding\":\"This call itself hit the platform's 120-second proxy timeout — the unresponsiveness investigation was still unresolved when time ran out.\"},{\"source\":\"attempt termination record\",\"finding\":\"Cluster lease expired at 14:57:07, shortly after the last (still-timing-out) diagnostic command at 14:56:39.\"}],\"likely_causes\":[{\"cause\":\"RabbitMQ/Erlang signing-key and repo-setup URLs (raw.githubusercontent.com paths, Cloudsmith setup.rpm.sh) were stale, wrong, or unreachable from this environment, forcing a manual/undocumented repo-file workaround that itself then exceeded the exec proxy timeout.\",\"confidence\":\"medium\"},{\"cause\":\"The dnf install of erlang+rabbitmq-server legitimately took longer than 120 seconds (likely due to EPEL/Cloudsmith dependency resolution or slow mirrors) and was run as a single blocking exec instead of the platform's recommended background+poll pattern, causing a false 'failed' result even though the install ultimately succeeded.\",\"confidence\":\"medium\"},{\"cause\":\"A classic (non-quorum) test queue (tls_test_q) became unresponsive after node1 was rebooted mid-session — likely a general RabbitMQ classic-queue/Mnesia resync characteristic on restart rather than a TLS-specific issue — and repeated rabbitmqctl polling against it consumed the remaining time budget until the lease expired before recovery could be confirmed.\",\"confidence\":\"medium\"},{\"cause\":\"The observed bad_certificate/selfsigned_peer TLS alert is very likely an intentional negative test (client presenting a non-CA cert being correctly rejected) rather than a misconfiguration, but the evidence does not include a matching positive test showing a CA-issued client cert succeeding, so mTLS enforcement is only half-verified.\",\"confidence\":\"low\"}],\"next_attempt_guidance\":[\"Before attempting package installation, verify outbound reachability to the RabbitMQ/Erlang key and repo hosts (raw.githubusercontent.com, dl.cloudsmith.io, github.com release assets) with a plain curl -I/-v probe on one node first, rather than looping through multiple bootstrap methods live.\",\"Run `dnf install -y erlang rabbitmq-server` using the primer's background+poll pattern (`cmd > /tmp/out.log 2>&1 & echo $! > /tmp/pid`, then `tail` in follow-up execs) instead of a single blocking exec, to avoid false failures from the 120-second proxy timeout.\",\"After installing, explicitly verify TLS mutual-auth from both directions: attempt one client connection using a certificate signed by the cluster CA (expect success) and one with a cert not signed by that CA or no cert (expect rejection) — capture both outcomes rather than relying on an incidental log line.\",\"For any test queues, prefer quorum queues (not classic) if the plan includes rebooting a node, since classic queues on a single node showed post-reboot unresponsiveness in this attempt; if classic queues are required by the task, confirm they recover fully (rabbitmqctl list_queues returns promptly) before moving on, and budget extra time for that check.\",\"Confirm firewalld rules for the management port (15672) and inter-node ports are applied with --permanent (or otherwise persisted) so they survive a reboot, and re-check firewall-cmd --list-all after any reboot.\",\"Track elapsed time against the lease window explicitly — this attempt spent roughly the first 5 minutes on repo/signing-key troubleshooting and the last several minutes stuck on queue-unresponsiveness diagnostics with no successful conclusion before expiry; leave a time buffer to finish validation and produce a final status report before the lease is likely to end.\"]}","structured_output":{"summary":"Executor eventually got a 3-node RabbitMQ cluster running with AMQP-TLS on 5671 and management restricted to the cluster subnet, but spent a large share of the session fighting package-repo/signing-key fetch failures, then a rabbitmqctl-observed queue-unresponsiveness problem surfaced right after a self-triggered node1 reboot, and the cluster lease expired (14:57:07) while that was still being investigated — so final validated state (e.g. a CA-issued client actually connecting, and the queue fully recovering) is not confirmed in the evidence.","evidence":[{"source":"node2/node3 rpm -q check at 14:37:22","finding":"rabbitmq-server and erlang were not pre-installed; executor had to install from scratch on all 3 nodes."},{"source":"node1/node2/node3 curl to raw.githubusercontent.com signing keys, 14:37:52-14:38:06","finding":"epel-release installed fine, but the combined command returned exit code 1 and a follow-up ls found no rabbit/cloudsmith key files — the signing-key curls failed silently."},{"source":"cloudsmith setup.rpm.sh curl+bash on all 3 nodes, 14:38:19-14:38:21","finding":"return_code 22 (curl -f HTTP error) on all three nodes — the Cloudsmith bootstrap script URL was unreachable or erroring."},{"source":"node1 custom repo file + rpm --import + dnf install, 14:41:45","finding":"Command failed with a 120-second proxy read timeout (AntriebMCPError), i.e. the install ran long enough to exceed the exec proxy limit; the redacted base64 blob content is unknown."},{"source":"node1 systemctl is-active rabbitmq-server, 14:52:16","finding":"Despite the earlier timeout error, rabbitmq-server was later found 'active', implying the install (or a retry) succeeded in the background after the timed-out exec call."},{"source":"node1 rabbit@node1.log tail, 14:51:27","finding":"TLS handshake failure logged: {tls_alert,{bad_certificate,...,\"selfsigned_peer\"}} for a peer at 10.100.149.10:44550 — consistent with the cluster correctly rejecting a client cert not issued by the configured CA."},{"source":"node1 firewall-cmd --list-all, 14:51:36","finding":"Port 5671/tcp open publicly (matches AMQP-TLS client access requirement); rich rules restrict 25672, 15672, 4369 to source 10.100.149.0/24 only (matches 'management reachable only within cluster' requirement). No --permanent flag evidence, so persistence across reboot is unconfirmed."},{"source":"node2 curl to node1:15672 via ssh, 14:51:31","finding":"200 OK from within the cluster subnet, confirming management UI is reachable from cluster peers as intended."},{"source":"node1 boot_id/uptime before and after reboot, 14:51:40-14:52:14","finding":"Executor deliberately rebooted node1 (systemctl reboot); node came back up within ~30s and rejoined the cluster (rabbit@node1/node2/node3 all listed as Running Nodes at 14:52:18)."},{"source":"node1 rabbitmqctl list_queues, 14:53:21 and 14:56:36","finding":"Both calls hit RabbitMQ's own internal 60-second timeout with 'Some queue(s) are unresponsive' for tls_test_q, despite the queue separately being reported as state=running."},{"source":"node1 rabbitmqctl list_unresponsive_queues, 14:55:29","finding":"This call itself hit the platform's 120-second proxy timeout — the unresponsiveness investigation was still unresolved when time ran out."},{"source":"attempt termination record","finding":"Cluster lease expired at 14:57:07, shortly after the last (still-timing-out) diagnostic command at 14:56:39."}],"likely_causes":[{"cause":"RabbitMQ/Erlang signing-key and repo-setup URLs (raw.githubusercontent.com paths, Cloudsmith setup.rpm.sh) were stale, wrong, or unreachable from this environment, forcing a manual/undocumented repo-file workaround that itself then exceeded the exec proxy timeout.","confidence":"medium"},{"cause":"The dnf install of erlang+rabbitmq-server legitimately took longer than 120 seconds (likely due to EPEL/Cloudsmith dependency resolution or slow mirrors) and was run as a single blocking exec instead of the platform's recommended background+poll pattern, causing a false 'failed' result even though the install ultimately succeeded.","confidence":"medium"},{"cause":"A classic (non-quorum) test queue (tls_test_q) became unresponsive after node1 was rebooted mid-session — likely a general RabbitMQ classic-queue/Mnesia resync characteristic on restart rather than a TLS-specific issue — and repeated rabbitmqctl polling against it consumed the remaining time budget until the lease expired before recovery could be confirmed.","confidence":"medium"},{"cause":"The observed bad_certificate/selfsigned_peer TLS alert is very likely an intentional negative test (client presenting a non-CA cert being correctly rejected) rather than a misconfiguration, but the evidence does not include a matching positive test showing a CA-issued client cert succeeding, so mTLS enforcement is only half-verified.","confidence":"low"}],"next_attempt_guidance":["Before attempting package installation, verify outbound reachability to the RabbitMQ/Erlang key and repo hosts (raw.githubusercontent.com, dl.cloudsmith.io, github.com release assets) with a plain curl -I/-v probe on one node first, rather than looping through multiple bootstrap methods live.","Run `dnf install -y erlang rabbitmq-server` using the primer's background+poll pattern (`cmd > /tmp/out.log 2>&1 & echo $! > /tmp/pid`, then `tail` in follow-up execs) instead of a single blocking exec, to avoid false failures from the 120-second proxy timeout.","After installing, explicitly verify TLS mutual-auth from both directions: attempt one client connection using a certificate signed by the cluster CA (expect success) and one with a cert not signed by that CA or no cert (expect rejection) — capture both outcomes rather than relying on an incidental log line.","For any test queues, prefer quorum queues (not classic) if the plan includes rebooting a node, since classic queues on a single node showed post-reboot unresponsiveness in this attempt; if classic queues are required by the task, confirm they recover fully (rabbitmqctl list_queues returns promptly) before moving on, and budget extra time for that check.","Confirm firewalld rules for the management port (15672) and inter-node ports are applied with --permanent (or otherwise persisted) so they survive a reboot, and re-check firewall-cmd --list-all after any reboot.","Track elapsed time against the lease window explicitly — this attempt spent roughly the first 5 minutes on repo/signing-key troubleshooting and the last several minutes stuck on queue-unresponsiveness diagnostics with no successful conclusion before expiry; leave a time buffer to finish validation and produce a final status report before the lease is likely to end."]},"ttft_ms":38689,"type":"result","duration_ms":84926,"uuid":"ef762d6d-b198-4b61-9539-91a453e3e882","ttft_stream_ms":890,"time_to_request_ms":35,"first_content_frame_ms":1521,"queued_turn_count":0}
